# Build artifacts
claude
cli-runnable.js
source.js
deobfuscated/
.deob_cache/
.build-state.json

# Compiled binaries built alongside the live one. `claude` above matches ONLY the
# exact name, so every parked/backup build is untracked-but-not-ignored and shows
# up as a `??` staging candidate — 601 MB of them as of 2026-09-03.
#
# 🔴 THE EXPLICIT LIST DID NOT HOLD. It enumerated the names that existed at the
# time (claude-2.1.*, claude-test, claude-prev-*, claude-rel*) and every build
# named afterwards escaped it: claude-238-*, claude-259/260/261-*, claude-263-*,
# claude-pre-refetch. Measured 2026-09-21: 25 binaries, ~2.8 GB, all `??` again —
# the exact condition this block was added to end. A pattern that must be
# extended by hand every time someone parks a build is not a rule, it is a
# reminder, and it was not read.
#
# So: ignore the whole prefix and carve out the one tracked exception. That is
# what the original note rejected `claude-*` for; the negation covers it, and
# `git ls-files | grep ^claude` confirms it is the only one.
claude-*
!claude-renamer.md
*.backup

# TS build
tools-ts/node_modules/

# Version reference (large binary files, download separately)
versionref/

# Handoff (contains local tokens/paths)
HANDOFF.md

# TS lock
tools-ts/bun.lock
.DS_Store

# Assets extracted from the upstream binary (2.1.242+ chunked builds embed .md/
# .txt/.node in a bun VFS). Same status as versionref/: copyrighted upstream
# content, reproducible from the source binary via tools/extract_assets.py, so
# never committed.
*.node
*-[0-9a-z][0-9a-z][0-9a-z][0-9a-z][0-9a-z][0-9a-z][0-9a-z][0-9a-z].md
*-[0-9a-z][0-9a-z][0-9a-z][0-9a-z][0-9a-z][0-9a-z][0-9a-z][0-9a-z].txt
*.txt.zst
# `.mjs` joined this set when extract_assets.py's positional pass raised
# uncompressed text recovery from 7/76 to 74/76 — the newly-recovered names
# include runner-scaffold-<hash>.mjs and build-report-lite-<hash>.mjs, which
# had simply never been extracted before. Same provenance, same rule.
*-[0-9a-z][0-9a-z][0-9a-z][0-9a-z][0-9a-z][0-9a-z][0-9a-z][0-9a-z].mjs

# Python bytecode from tools/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
